Subject: [PATCH] Destroy the native viewer adapter on its owning UI thread

Applies to ros-controls/mujoco_ros2_control tag 0.1.2

The native viewer is constructed on ui_thread_, but sim_ is destroyed by
the controller-manager thread after shutdown joins ui_thread_. Leaving the
adapter in sim_ therefore calls GlfwAdapter::~GlfwAdapter without its GL
context current, and mjr_freeContext can crash in libGLdispatch on Linux

Release only the adapter immediately after RenderLoop, while its window
and GL context still belong to the UI thread. GlfwAdapter can then free
the MuJoCo rendering context, detach the GL context and destroy the GLFW
window in the original order. Retain Simulate and the physics state until
the existing shutdown/join sequence completes

diff --git a/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp b/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp
--- a/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp
+++ b/mujoco_ros2_control/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp
@@ -626,6 +626,11 @@ bool MujocoSimulation::initialize(rclcpp::Node::SharedPtr node, const std::string&
       RCLCPP_INFO(get_logger(), "Starting the MuJoCo rendering thread...");
       sim_->RenderLoop();
 
+      // Destroy GL resources on the thread that owns the current context,
+      // before it exits or ROS shutdown lets another thread destroy sim_.
+      // Physics uses Simulate's state, not its platform UI adapter.
+      sim_->platform_ui.reset();
+
       if (detail::handle_render_loop_exit(sim_->exitrequest, explicit_shutdown_requested_,
                                           node_->get_node_base_interface()->get_context()))
       {
